From: Bellatrix contributors
Subject: [PATCH] test/smp: build libatomic before linking SmallPT

TARGET_CXX_LDFLAGS makes the C++ link request libatomic on targets that need
it, but the SmallPT target does not order the corresponding link library into
the build. A clean full m68k distribution therefore reaches the test before
libatomic exists and fails with "cannot find -latomic".

Declare the dependency directly on the program target, as the Mesa and Gallium
users already do. Placing it only on the test-smp aggregate would leave its
children unordered and could still run the link first.

---
 developer/debug/test/smp/smp-smallpt/mmakefile.src | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/developer/debug/test/smp/smp-smallpt/mmakefile.src b/developer/debug/test/smp/smp-smallpt/mmakefile.src
index 1f29ebed26..cd7c753cdf 100644
--- a/developer/debug/test/smp/smp-smallpt/mmakefile.src
+++ b/developer/debug/test/smp/smp-smallpt/mmakefile.src
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ EXEDIR  := $(AROS_TESTS)/smp
 
 #MM- test-smp : test-smp-smp-smallpt
 #MM- test-smp-quick : test-smp-smp-smallpt-quick
+#MM test-smp-smp-smallpt : linklibs-libatomic
 
 #USER_CFLAGS := $(PARANOIA_CFLAGS)
 
-- 
